  "details": "Just like other social platforms, Follow or Connect can be useful to avoid the awkwardness that implies being Friends when actually not being friends. Friend is a meaningful and powerful word and can be interpreted in many ways.\n\nWith a Follow or Connect button someone could subscribe to get notified of your status, world that you are in, Public instance that you created and other things.\n\nAdding, UnFriending and even lagging through a huge list of friends can be overwhelming.\n\nSome friendships are not really relevant and you might delete them because you never really hangout, some friendships are not actually needed just because you had a good time sharing together drunk at Drinking Night. Sometimes you are just not looking for more friends that you have to scroll through to find your closest friends.\n\nI don't recall seeing Friends Location menu having a feature to only show Favorite friends locations? (Please tell me if I'm wrong). And avoid lagging or scrolling a lot.\n\nSometimes it can be awkward rejecting friend requests if the other person notices.\n\nSome people are very likeable or popular and get a lot of friends request but they are just not in the mood, or add an option to disable Incoming Friend Request to avoid people adding you randomly with no prior interaction or avoiding people taking it personal if they don't get their friend requests accepted.\n\nI once deleted many friends that we never hangout with or don't even remember (mostly from drinking night) and once we met again by accident things got awkward.\n\nPlease at this button or feature.",
